+# CONTRACT.md — T8 Analytics Dashboard
+
+Derived from `tests/*.test.ts` (source of truth) and `.thunderdome/rubric.yaml`.
+
+## Core infrastructure
+
+- [x] `src/db.ts` exports `setDb(db)`, `getDb()`, `createTestDb()`, `closeDb()`.
+      `createTestDb()` returns an in-memory better-sqlite3 DB with `schema.sql` applied.
+      verify: every unit test file imports these and runs against them.
+- [x] `src/errors.ts` exports `errorHandler` (express error middleware) and typed error classes.
+      All error responses are `{ error: string, code: string }`.
+      verify: integration.test.ts "consistent error format for missing auth" / "invalid token".
+- [x] `src/auth/middleware.ts` (or similar) — shared JWT auth middleware used by all protected routers.
+      Sets `req.user = { id, tenantId }` from a verified JWT.
+      Missing token → 401 `{error, code}`. Invalid token → 401 `{error, code: 'AUTH_ERROR'}`.
+      verify: integration.test.ts auth error tests.
+- [x] JWT shape `{ sub, tid, iat, exp }` — `sub` = user id, `tid` = tenant id.
+      verify: integration.test.ts "should return JWT with correct shape".
+- [x] `src/app.ts` exports `createApp()` building the full express app, wiring all routers + auth + errorHandler.
+      verify: integration.test.ts imports `createApp`.
+- [x] Passwords hashed (bcrypt or similar), never stored/returned plaintext.
+      verify: rubric llm_rubric criterion; users.unit.test login tests imply hash compare.
+
+## 1. Users (`src/users/router.ts`, default export express.Router)
+
+- [x] `POST /users` — body `{email, password, tenant_id}` → 201 `{id, email, tenant_id, role: 'viewer', ...}` (no password/hash in response).
+      Duplicate email → 409.
+      verify: users.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts.
+- [x] `POST /users/login` — body `{email, password}` → 200 `{token, user: {email,...}}`.
+      Wrong password → 401.
+      verify: users.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts.
+- [x] `GET /users/me` — requires auth (req.user set) → 200 user profile (own user).
+      verify: users.unit.test.ts (mock auth), integration full workflow.
+- [x] `PATCH /users/:id/role` — admin only → 200 updated user `{role}`.
+      Non-admin → 403 (implied, not explicitly tested but required by description).
+      verify: users.unit.test.ts "admin to change user role".
+
+## 2. Ingest (`src/ingest/router.ts`)
+
+- [x] `POST /events` — requires auth. body `{name, properties?, timestamp?, session_id?}`.
+      tenant_id derived from `req.user.tenantId`, NOT from body.
+      Missing `name` → 400. Success → 201 with full event incl. `id`, `tenant_id`, `name`, `timestamp`.
+      Custom timestamp echoed back exactly.
+      verify: ingest.unit.test.ts.
+- [x] `POST /events/batch` — body `{events: [...]}`. Empty array → 400.
+      Success → 201 `{inserted: N, events: [...]}`.
+      verify: ingest.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts.
+
+## 3. Query (`src/query/router.ts`) — all require auth, all scoped to req.user.tenantId
+
+- [x] `POST /query/count` — body `{event_name, start?, end?}`. Missing `event_name` → 400.
+      → 200 `{count: N}`. start/end filter by timestamp range (inclusive).
+      verify: query.unit.test.ts.
+- [x] `POST /query/timeseries` — body `{event_name, bucket}` (bucket e.g. 'day').
+      → 200 `{data: [{bucket, count}, ...]}`.
+      verify: query.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts.
+- [x] `POST /query/breakdown` — body `{event_name, property_key}`.
+      → 200 `{data: [{property_value, count}, ...]}` grouped by JSON property.
+      verify: query.unit.test.ts (/home count=2).
+- [x] `POST /query/funnel` — body `{steps: [name1, name2, ...]}`.
+      → 200 `{steps: [{name, count}, ...]}` monotonically non-increasing counts
+      (funnel computed per session_id: each step's count = sessions that did this step AND all previous steps).
+      verify: query.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts funnel.
+- [x] Tenant isolation: tenant B never sees tenant A's events in any query.
+      verify: integration.test.ts "enforce tenant isolation in queries".
+
+## 4. Dashboards (`src/dashboards/router.ts`) — all require auth, scoped to tenant
+
+- [x] `POST /dashboards` — body `{name, config?}` → 201 dashboard incl. `id`, `tenant_id`, `name`, owner_id from req.user.id.
+- [x] `GET /dashboards` — → 200 array of tenant's dashboards only.
+- [x] `GET /dashboards/:id` — → 200 `{...dashboard, widgets: [...]}`. Not found / wrong tenant → 404.
+- [x] `PATCH /dashboards/:id` — body partial update (e.g. `{name}`) → 200 updated dashboard.
+- [x] `DELETE /dashboards/:id` — → 204. Subsequent GET → 404.
+- [x] `POST /dashboards/:id/widgets` — body `{type, config, position_x?, position_y?, width?, height?}`
+      type one of counter|timeseries|breakdown|funnel → 201 widget incl. `id`, `dashboard_id`.
+- [x] `DELETE /dashboards/:id/widgets/:widgetId` — → 204.
+      verify: dashboards.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts (widget add/delete, tenant isolation of dashboards).
+
+## 5. Export (`src/export/router.ts`) — all require auth, scoped to tenant
+
+- [x] `GET /export/events?format=json` — → 200 JSON array of tenant's events only.
+- [x] `GET /export/events?format=csv` — → 200, `content-type` contains `text/csv`, header row contains `id`,
+      `lines.length === N+1` (header + N events, trailing newline NOT adding an extra blank "line" beyond count, per test: 2 events → 3 lines when split by '\n' — i.e. no trailing newline, or split produces exactly header+2 rows with no trailing empty string).
+      verify: export.unit.test.ts (lines.length === 3 for 2 events, no trailing blank).
+- [x] Invalid format (anything other than csv/json) → 400.
+- [x] `GET /export/dashboard/:id` — → 200 `{dashboard, widgets: [...]}`. Not found / wrong tenant → 404.
+      verify: export.unit.test.ts, integration.test.ts (tenant isolation of export).
+
+## Global / cross-cutting
+
+- [x] `npm run build` (tsc, strict mode) compiles cleanly.
+- [x] `npm run lint` (eslint + @typescript-eslint/recommended) clean.
+- [x] `npm test` (vitest run) — all tests in tests/*.test.ts pass.
+- [x] No `any` left unhandled in ways that trip `@typescript-eslint/recommended` (no-explicit-any is not in recommended set by default — verify only no-unused-vars is enforced per .eslintrc.cjs, but be clean regardless).
